"""Per-message turn context for one engine turn.

Established once at the start of each engine turn and exposed through a
:class:`contextvars.ContextVar` so that any code running within the turn's
async call stack — the orchestrator, the skill executor, builder ``@tool``
functions — can emit agent responses and read turn state without threading
parameters through every method signature.

Why a context var (and what it deliberately does *not* carry)
-------------------------------------------------------------
Response emission flows *downward* from the turn coroutine into the output
channel, so an ambient ``ContextVar`` set at turn start is visible everywhere
it needs to be (including the audio-sender task spawned inside
``send_text_message`` for streaming voice).

Cancellation crosses task boundaries through a shared token: it stops
execution. A voice barge-in only mutes the output channel while the engine keeps
working. User input that arrives during the turn is taken in by the turn itself
(:meth:`MessageTurnContext.take_pending_input`) at the orchestrator's restart
points.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

